  Stored runs are long: at -4 -k 4096, 2468 runs averaging 4597 bytes,
  67% of them between 256 and 2047 bytes.

Findings:
  - only 29% (4 MB) to 33% (32 kB) of the input bytes are looked up at -4:
    the rest is covered by matches and passed over. The literal path
    handles 20-28% of the bytes, the reference path most of the rest;
  - 61% of references directly follow another one;
  - length 4 is 37% of the references, 9-16 still 13%;
  - distances are almost flat at 7-12% per power of two from 64 to 16k;
    at 32 kB the blocks cap them, so the last two buckets shrink;
  - at 4 MB, 8% of word hits are stale entries out of the window: lost
    bucket capacity. Not at 32 kB since the table is reset per block;
  - the text tree at 32 kB rejects 24% of the matches it finds, because
    of its debt limit (SLZ_TEXT_MAX_DEBT).


